-- The seat is the person the appointment and removal rules are applied to: a candidate for judicial office, and a judge whose term is
-- proposed to be ended. The committee, the Minister, the Knesset and the Court have no seat here; they appear only as what they do to that person.
--
-- Membership test for this module: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact (who sat, who voted for, on what day), or does
-- answering it require reading the Law? Only the first kind is here.

§ `Nouns of the Judicial Selection Committee`

§§ `Seats`

-- A seat is a place on the committee, by the description the Law gives it. Before the 26th Knesset (s 4(b) as it stood): the President of the Supreme Court,
-- two other justices, the Minister of Justice, another minister, two Knesset members, two representatives of the Bar. From the 26th Knesset (s 4(b)(1), (2)
-- as Amendment No. 4 s 1(1) put it): the Bar's two seats become two public representatives, and the two Knesset members become one of the coalition factions
-- and one of the opposition factions. Where the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members (s 4(f)(2)) both public representatives are chosen by the Knesset.
DECLARE `A seat on the committee` IS ONE OF
    `the President of the Supreme Court`
    `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`
    `the Minister of Justice`
    `another minister whom the Government names`
    `a representative of the Bar Association`
    `a Knesset member whom the Knesset chose`
    `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`
    `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`
    `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose`
    `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose`
    `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose`

-- One member serving on the committee, and whether that member votes in favour of the decision put. A tally is a list of these, one for each member SERVING: a member who is absent, or who does not vote in favour, is in the list with `votes in favour` FALSE, so that "all the members serving" (s 4B, Amendment No. 4 s 3) is counted against the whole list.
DECLARE `A member serving on the committee` HAS
    `the seat` IS A `A seat on the committee`
    `votes in favour` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The three paragraphs of s 4(d), which the decision rule counts by.
DECLARE `A paragraph of section 4(d)` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph 1, a judge`
    `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
    `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose`
    `none of the three paragraphs`

§§ `Vintages and kinds of decision`

-- Vintages are explicit and never merged. The transitional window is Amendment No. 4 s 3: from the first day of the 26th Knesset's term until a committee is set up under
-- the new text, the committee set up before commencement goes on under the old text, may not elect judges, and decides other matters with all serving members.
DECLARE `A vintage of the committee rule` IS ONE OF
    `the text before the 26th Knesset`
    `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
    `the text from the 26th Knesset`

DECLARE `A kind of decision of the committee` IS ONE OF
    `the election of a judge of a court other than the Supreme Court`
    `the election of a judge of the Supreme Court`
    `a decision that is not the election of a judge`

-- Who may put to the committee a proposal to end a judge's term (s 7(4)).
DECLARE `Who proposes to end a judge's term` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee`
    `the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges`
    `the President of the Supreme Court`
    `someone else`

§§ `Days`

-- A day by its parts, because the Law counts "a year" and "a month" from a day (s 4A(a), (d)).
DECLARE `A calendar day` HAS
    `the day of the month` IS A NUMBER
    `the month` IS A NUMBER
    `the year` IS A NUMBER

-- The days that start a period in which the committee may not elect judges (s 4B). A day the Law does not make relevant is NOTHING.
DECLARE `The days relevant to section 4B` HAS
    `the day of the Knesset elections under s 9 of Basic Law: The Knesset` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day a ground for elections arose under s 34 or 36A of Basic Law: The Knesset, or s 11(b) or 29(f) of Basic Law: The Government` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the Government resigned under s 18, 19, 20, 21 or 29(a) of Basic Law: The Government` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day the Knesset decided to express no confidence in the Government under s 28 of Basic Law: The Government` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day members were chosen in place of the members named in s 4(b)(1)(b) to (d)` IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `Cross-references`

-- What a provision deals with, in the words of its own heading or of the citing text. A cross-reference is a pair of these: what the CITING text says
-- the target is, and what the TARGET says it is. A test asks whether the two agree.
DECLARE `What a provision deals with` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court judge majority of section 4(e)`
    `the ordinary decision majority of section 4(d)`
    `paragraph 2 of section 4(d)`
    `paragraph 3 of section 4(d)`
    `the appointment of a judge by the President of the State on the committee's election`
    `the members of the committee other than the judges: the ministers, the Knesset members and the public representatives`
    `the two public representatives of section 4(b)(1)(d)`
    `the date of regular elections to the Knesset`
    `dissolution of the Knesset by law`
    `dissolution for want of a budget law`
    `early elections when no Government is formed`
    `elections when the Prime Minister's dissolution order is not followed by a Government`
    `the Government resigns or is deemed to have resigned`
    `the Knesset expresses no confidence in the Government`
    `ending a judge's term by decision of the committee`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing provision` IS A STRING
    `the cited provision` IS A STRING
    `what the citing text says it points at` IS A `What a provision deals with`
    `what the cited provision deals with` IS A `What a provision deals with`
